reviews.factual_errors:
1. The floor rule n = floor(refresh*1.01/pace) makes latency worse than today whenever refresh/pace is 2 or more and not an integer. SCK then delivers just above the pace, so each taken picture waits for the grid. Today SCK runs at max_fps, often every vsync. Model (strict gating; /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lb7666--claude-spares-spare-vPIbq7/2de9709e-ea4b-442d-a692-7f9e8fd50cdd/scratchpad/notes/r1review/rule_model.py), time from a change to its capture, today's every-vsync delivery against the floor rule:
   - 60 Hz pace 25: 23.0 vs 31.6 ms;
   - 120 Hz pace 45: 13.4 vs 16.4 ms;
   - 144 Hz pace 50: 12.9 vs 16.4 ms;
   - 144 Hz pace 30: 19.6 vs 29.3 ms;
   - 100 Hz pace 30: 19.7 vs 29.7 ms.
   Such paces are common: Balanced's normal is 45 (qos.rs:111-118), and congestion adapts the pace.
2. 'As many thread C wakes are saved' is wrong. The SCK callback wakes thread C only for the first picture after a take (capture.rs:138-147, wake = !latest.fresh). Surplus frames cost SCK/WindowServer GPU work and one dispatch callback each, but at most one thread C wake per tick.
3. Changing fields of the configuration kept in Running while an earlier updateConfiguration may still be reading it is not safe; airhand does this (capture/sck.rs:318-324).

