missed.design:
Why: the shared stream follows the lowest limits among active viewers (worker/capture.rs:211-228). Any change of those limits makes thread C call configure_video (269-281). PlatformBackend::configure_video drops the source unconditionally (native.rs:151-156), so the next capture:
- re-enumerates SCShareableContent;
- restarts the SCK stream;
- rebuilds VideoToolbox;
- waits for the first Complete picture.

Viewers' default limits are the Native bounds (video.rs:137, 3840x2160 for everyone) at their own refresh. So in a room, the common difference is fps alone: a 60 Hz phone and a 120 Hz Mac. Every pause or resume of the phone (app backgrounded), and every join or leave, then rebuilds capture for the other viewer and freezes their picture for the restart.

Design:
1. platform/mod.rs VideoSource: a provided `fn retune(&mut self, display: &Display, limits: VideoLimits) -> Result<bool> { Ok(false) }`. It returns true when the source now serves `limits` without a rebuild.
2. native.rs configure_video: validate the limits, then
   - if a source is open and `video.retune(&context.display, limits)` returns Ok(true), keep it;
   - otherwise drop it, as today;
   - store the limits either way.
   A context change still rebuilds, because capture_video compares the context (native.rs:191-206).
3. MacVideo::retune:
   - return false unless scaled_size(display, new limits) equals its own encode size;
   - otherwise store max_fps (the cadence fallback);
   - set kVTCompressionPropertyKey_ExpectedFrameRate live, best effort, since it is a hint;
   - re-apply the SCK cadence for the current pace (R1-sck-interval-follows-pace);
   - return true.
4. Thread C is unchanged. It still sets keyframe on a limits change, because the joining or resuming viewer needs that IDR anyway.
5. Windows keeps the default (a rebuild) until its own area decides whether its MF encoder can keep its media type.
6. Tests:
   - a PlatformBackend test over the synthetic platform: SynVideo implements retune; an fps-only change opens no new source, and a size change opens one;
   - a worker test that a paused second slot with lower fps keeps the source.
7. Docs: the 'Remote resolution' / shared-stream text and the host paragraph.

