candidates.protocol:
HELPER_PROTOCOL 11, with `pb-mapper.desktop-helper.v11` and `pb-mapper.desktop-background.v11`.

Between replies the worker may send tagged records, all deny_unknown_fields:
- `{kind:"unit", generation, video: VideoFormat, pending}` followed by its bytes record;
- `{kind:"fresh", presented_ago_us}`;
- `{kind:"pointer", cursor, shape_serial}`.

Replies are tagged `{kind:"reply", ...Response}`. Request gains `Stream{on, hot_ms}`.

Both ends validate:
- a unit is at most ipc::MAX_FRAME;
- its generation must match the host's expected context;
- pending is at most 64;
- the pointer lies inside the display.

Desktop wire and ALPN: unchanged.

