candidates.change:
video/mod.rs:
- The duplication moves to a capture thread owned by the Encoder. build() (249-369) spawns it. The thread:
  - calls CoInitializeEx(MTA);
  - calls SetThreadDesktop with the building thread's GetThreadDesktop, so it sits on the desktop thread C is bound to (helper/binding.rs:240-282, Winlogon included);
  - creates the DxgiDuplicationApi there (280-281);
  - hands thread C the multithread-protected device and context (643-646).
- Thread C arms it when its tick is due.
- Armed, the thread blocks in AcquireNextFrame (at most 16 ms, against 0 at 575). On a present it:
  - converts at once with the video processor into an NV12 ring of 6 encoded-size textures (SAMPLES.1). The slot with the newest picture and slots still in the encoder are never overwritten; outputs are FIFO;
  - releases the frame and flushes;
  - publishes (slot, present Instant from LastPresentTime);
  - calls the Waker.
- Unarmed, it waits on an event, and DXGI accumulates meanwhile.
- submit wraps the slot with MFCreateDXGISurfaceBuffer + MFCreateSample (as airhand mf.rs:749-762) and calls ProcessInput. A repeat or keyframe on a still desktop resubmits the newest slot.
- Errors, such as ACCESS_LOST on a desktop switch, are published and returned by the next submit as today.
- Drop sets stop and joins in at most 16 ms. native.rs:83-90 drops the video before rebinding.

