reviews.effect_assessment:
Real, for every privileged Windows session. "Turn on remote control" selects Access::Privileged (ui/native/pb_mapper_ffi/src/desktop/host.rs:521-525), the recommended setup. It brings:
- unit delivery about 0.3-1 ms sooner;
- no input queued behind a drain long-poll, which removes a 0-4 ms input delay;
- pipe round trips while active falling from up to about 500/s to about one per new picture plus pushes. Each of today's round trips crosses two pipes and the service relay and costs 3-5 desktop verifications plus AcquireNextFrame in the worker.

The CPU saving across app, service and worker is plausible at a few percent of a core while active, but unmeasured.

