candidates.pb_current:
platform/windows/input.rs:53-58 moves with SetCursorPos, because enigo's absolute move reaches only the primary screen. Buttons, wheel and text use enigo's SendInput, one call per event (:59-84). SetCursorPos repositions the cursor without an input event, which has four consequences:
- no WM_INPUT for raw-input apps;
- no WH_MOUSE_LL hook call;
- no reset of the idle timer read by GetLastInputInfo;
- no wake of a display that is off.

