not_worth_it.reason:
pb-mapper's video is TLS over one byte stream from connect_tcp or the loopback dial, and relay TCP and LAN TCP can carry only one stream.

On direct QUIC, an ordered stream already buffers what arrives after a loss and releases it when the retransmission lands. Without LTR nothing decodes sooner on separate streams; airhand itself waits 1.5 RTT + 30 ms before acting (merge.rs loss_wait).

It would also need:
- new SDK surface;
- raised stream limits through a relayed direct field;
- exporter-keyed AEAD outside the pinned TLS;
- a rewrite of credit, receipts and ordering.

missed.design:
The host Room keeps one record:
- the bpf of the last session that ended by transport loss (End::Closed or HOST_READ_TIMEOUT), relative to 1080p;
- its preset;
- when it ended.

A session accepted within 2 min starts with bpf = min(the preset's start, the remembered bpf). Qos::new takes an optional start. Balanced's fps fast start is unchanged.

No protocol change. A record older than 2 min, or from another preset, is ignored.

