reviews.corrected_design:
Host, as proposed: while capturing, cursor_due = now + CURSOR_INTERVAL.min(self.pacer.period()).max(8 ms).

Dart: keep the 16 ms timer as the idle fallback, but read at vsync while a peer pointer moves:
- when a leaf read (timer or frame) finds the peer cursors changed, call SchedulerBinding.instance.scheduleFrame(), so the next read runs in _onFrame at the display's rate;
- keep scheduling while successive reads change;
- stop when one finds no change.

Tests:
- a worker test: samples every period at pace 120 and every 16 ms at 60;
- a store test with simulated frames: a moving peer cursor is read every frame, and a still one only on the timer.

